# Copy to .env and fill in. Everything the instance needs from you lives here.
# The full setup guide — the Slack manifest, the scopes, and the documented traps —
# arrives with build/13.

# From your own Slack app (create it from the manifest; do not use a shared app).
# Bot User OAuth Token, under OAuth & Permissions.
SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=xoxb-...
# App-Level Token with connections:write, under Basic Information. Socket Mode.
SLACK_APP_TOKEN=xapp-...

# Optional. Defaults are in src/config.ts.
# VAULT_DIR=./vault
# WORKSPACE_ROOT=./.workspaces
# The instance's own durable state — only which Session each Thread resumes into.
# Delete it and every Thread starts over as if it had never spoken to you.
# STATE_DIR=./.state
# OPERATING_MANUAL_PATH=./assets/operating-manual.md
# CODEX_MODEL=gpt-5.6-sol
# CODEX_REASONING_EFFORT=low
# The `codex` on PATH is used by default, falling back to the copy in node_modules.
# CODEX_PATH=/usr/local/bin/codex

# What stops a Job that does not stop by itself. Codex has no limits of its own — no
# timeout, no cap on turns, no budget, no kill switch — so these are the only ones
# there are. The defaults are deliberately generous enough for real work and tight
# enough that a runaway is an annoyance rather than a bill. Lower them freely.
#
# Wall clock on a single turn. A whole job is normally one turn, so this is in
# practice the ceiling on a job. Expiring kills the engine's process.
# TURN_TIMEOUT_MS=3600000
# How many turns one job may run before it is stopped. Catches a job that loops.
# MAX_TURNS_PER_JOB=8
# Cumulative tokens across a job, counted as the engine reports them. A ceiling on
# volume rather than on money — the instance does not know what your model costs.
# TOKEN_BUDGET_PER_JOB=1000000
# How many jobs run at once across every thread — the one bound on the instance rather
# than on a single job. One thread runs one job at a time whatever this says; this is
# what stops ten busy threads becoming ten subprocesses and ten of every budget above.
# Four sits just inside Slack's rate limit for editing progress messages.
# MAX_CONCURRENT_JOBS=4
